<title>FRANCE: Seita shares transfered to CCF, Sofinamm.</title>
<headline>Seita shares transfered to CCF, Sofinamm.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>French tobacco group Seita said on Tuesday that 2.5 percent of its shares had been transfered to Credit Commercial de France and another 2.5 percent to the Sofinamm group.</p>
<p>In a statement Seita said that the transfer came after the Nobel Elysees company jointly-owned by CCF and Sofinamm, was dissolved on April 30. Nobel Elysees had been set up to acquire a five percent stake in Seita.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +331 4221 5432</p>
